WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.667
I'm so happy to have you on.
-Thank you, Jimmy.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:04.968
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.834
-I've seen you at "SNL,"
I've seen you in the hallways,

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.000
but I've never had
you as a guest and I'm --

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.367
-And you've never said
a word to me.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.501
-I know.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:11.901
I like
to keep it really cool,

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:14.000
keep the mystique happening.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.067
But, finally, you're here.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.200
How's the week
going with Quinta?

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.334
-It's going great.

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:18.968
I think it's going to be
a really great show.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:21.300
Quinta is so funny, so talented.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.934
We had table read yesterday.
-Good.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.701
-I think she's got it on lock.
-Yeah, yeah. Good.

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:26.868
And how about you?
Let's talk about you.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.167
-Quinta is going to have
a really great show.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.300
-Yeah.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.534
-She's going to be amazing.
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:34.834
I think it'll be fun for me.
I'll be in the show for sure.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.000
We have a pretty big cast.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.067
-Do you know,
when I was on the show,

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.067
when I was a featured player,

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.467
they had a rule that
if you weren't in the show,

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.601
they would take you
even out of the credits.

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:44.033
-That is messed up.

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:47.033
-So I would call my mom like,
"I'm not in the show at all.

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.701
Like I'm not even
in the credits."

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:50.467
-I hate that for you.
-Like, "Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:51.534
I wasn't even --
-Like, they skipped right to --

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:52.868
-No, they skipped
right over that.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:55.767
-To the "G" last names?
-Exactly. Yeah. Completely.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:56.767
It was rough.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.434
-My mom called me
a few weeks ago

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:01.200
in the middle of the show
and was like,

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.767
"Hey, did you not
go to work tonight?

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:03.834
I don't see you."

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:06.901
-Oh, my God. It's rough.
It's rough, man.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.267
-I said, "I'm here.
-"Yeah, I'm here.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.334
I'm just not in the show
at all."

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:10.434
-But at least
I'm in the credits.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:11.601
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:12.701
At least you got the credits.
-Fooled her.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:13.901
That's the thing about
it, though.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.100
The credits -- if you're not
in the credits,

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.601
your mom knows
not to expect you in the show.

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:19.334
-Yeah. Then she's like, "This is
the best episode I ever saw."

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:21.133
You go, "Hey, I'm not in it."
Yeah.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:22.434
I was talking to you backstage.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:25.067
Because it was, like,
a kind of a sports-themed night.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:26.167
We're talking about
March Madness.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.000
And I said,
"Did you play any sports?"

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.300
You played a little basketball?

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.868
-I was going to say,
I played a little ballet.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.934
Yes, I was a ballerina
for 10 years,

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:34.033
but I played
a little basketball.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:36.267
I had a short-lived
basketball career.

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:38.434
-How short was it?
-It was three games.

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:39.567
-There you go.
-Yeah.

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:42.467
-That counts.
-Exactly three games long.

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.601
So, I have to get this
off of my chest.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.100
So, back in L.A.,
when I was coming up in improv,

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.067
there was this
all-female basketball league,

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:53.701
and a lot of the sketch
and improv players

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:56.200
were on this team
and on this league, right?

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.334
And it was highly coveted to be
in one of the teams, right?

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:02.033
But there were no spots.
There were never spots.

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.467
And it was like,
"Darn, you missed out."

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:06.067
So, a spot opened up,
and everyone was e-mailing,

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.367
being like,
"I want in, I want in."

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.767
I e-mailed.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:11.701
I got a response immediately
that's like, "We want you."

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:15.367
And I have to believe
it's because I'm black.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.601
I think they thought
I'd be good at basketball.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:17.968
But here's the thing.

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.968
I also thought I'd be good
at basketball because I'm black.

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:21.434
Don't work that way.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.267
It don't work that way.
-It doesn't work -- No.

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:25.601
-Turns out
it don't work that way.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.167
-Do you know anything
about basketball?

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:30.000
-I know what traveling is.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.734
-Oh, my gosh. Doesn't count.

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.934
-The very first game,
the other team,

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.434
I saw them sort of size
me up like,

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.200
"Oh, shoot,
The Traveling Pants have --"

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.834
That was our team name,
Traveling Pants.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.968
But we weren't Traveling because
we know that's not allowed.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:43.400
-Oh, okay. Yeah, yeah.
Good. You know that.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.901
-So, the other team,
I saw them size me up like,

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:47.901
"Oh, shoot, they got a,
like, tallish black girl.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.634
We're going to have to
look out for her," right?

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:50.767
First play happens.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.734
I'm assuming
that's what it's called.

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:55.100
And I get out on the court.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.801
This is real.
-"First play."

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.033
-Is that not what it's --
Tell me.

00:02:58.033 --> 00:02:59.834
-No.
-Okay. Very cool. Alright.

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:01.000
I really don't know
what I'm talking about.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.167
So, I get out on the court,

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:05.634
and the first whatever
it's called happens

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:08.868
and the ref starts screaming
at me to get out of the paint.

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:11.167
And I look at the court,
and I'm like,

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:12.434
"This whole thing is painted.

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:13.934
What is the paint?"

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:16.934
-There's nothing but paint.
Where do I go?

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:18.834
Am I traveling?
-Right. This is years later.

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:19.934
I still don't know
what the paint is.

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.000
-Okay.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.200
-I don't know what
the paint is,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.400
because, truly,
the whole thing is painted.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.601
Or is that real wood?
-Yeah, no. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.501
-Okay.
-The paint is under the rim.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:28.834
-Okay. Okay. Okay.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.734
Because I've heard songs
like, "I go hard in the paint,"

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:31.934
and I was just like,
"Yeah, cool."

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:33.367
I didn't know what it meant.
But now I know.

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:34.834
Okay, it's under the rim.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:38.234
So, anyway, I mean, people were
guarding me, like, arms up,

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.367
and my arms were up, too,

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:40.801
but mine meant like
"I surrender.

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.901
I am not a threat.

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:44.801
I'm not a threat."

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:47.167
I remember, like,
being wide open,

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:48.834
because everyone realized
very quickly,

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:49.901
I don't know what I'm doing.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:51.133
-Yeah.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.167
-"Actually, don't worry
about the black girl."

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:55.200
-No one was guarding you?
-Nobody was guarding me.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.033
And my team --
my teammate had the ball

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:58.367
and needed to pass it
to someone,

00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:00.467
and I was the only one
who was open.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:02.200
Arms were still up,
and I was like, "Don't do that.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.033
Please don't do that.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:05.501
Please don't do that."

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:07.400
-Could I tell you about you're
having such a fantastic season

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.868
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:10.200
I think I told --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.534
-Thank you. Thank you.
-Really. Fantastic.

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:13.868
-Thank you.

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:16.601
-The sketch I remember I was
e-mailing a bunch of --

00:04:16.601 --> 00:04:18.601
you know, Higgins and our
friends over at "SNL."

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:20.534
I said, "There's that sketch
last night,

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:23.534
'Lisa from Temecula,'"
where you were cutting --

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.367
you were cutting the steak
on the table,

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:27.634
and the table was shaking.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:31.400
Dude, it was unbelievably funny.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.501
It made me laugh out loud.
I go, "What is going on?"

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:36.934
I know those people
that kind of cut too much,

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.167
and the whole table
is shaking.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.901
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Walk me through it.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:43.234
Did you -- Do you know
someone who did this?

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:44.767
-You know, I used to be
a Lisa from Temecula,

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:47.667
except for I was an
Ego from Baltimore.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.901
I used to order my steaks
well-done.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.200
I got bullied out of it.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.434
People bullied me enough --
I stopped doing that.

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:55.868
But Alex English,

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.868
who wrote this sketch
alongside Gary Richardson,

00:04:57.868 --> 00:05:00.200
another writer, and
Michael Che -- people know --

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.400
his cousin
is a Lisa from Temecula,

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.934
is not from Temecula.

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:05.501
I don't know if she knows
it's about her,

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.334
so I might have blown his cover.

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:08.767
-Wow! Wow! It's happening.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.734
-But it is about his cousin,
who I guess he went to dinner

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:12.968
over one of our hiatuses,

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:14.300
and she had ordered her steak
well-done.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.601
It was kind of
shaking the table.

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:17.534
Only thing is, no one said
anything to her about it.

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:20.267
So I guess this was cathartic
and healing for him.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.567
-And did you know that
in dress rehearsal --

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.334
Like, sometimes, you go,
"Oh, I got a feeling

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:26.567
this is going to be
a fun, big sketch."

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:28.067
-Well, okay, so, all week long,

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:29.734
we had thought
it was going to be so exciting.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.200
I mean, when we did it
at table read,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.033
I couldn't -- They had a steak
delivered to me at table read,

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.834
and that doesn't happen.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.434
And Mikey Day and I,
by the way, have this bit

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:38.501
where he -- I think it's a bit.

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:39.634
I hope it's a bit.

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:41.834
Where he thinks I'm a diva.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:44.167
And someone delivered
a steak to me at our table read,

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:46.133
in the middle of our
table read, and he saw it.

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:47.834
Like, he saw it
and he was like, "What?!"

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:49.100
-"You really are a diva.
Wow! My God."

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.467
-Right, right. Truly.
So, the steak comes to me.

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:52.968
I'm doing it at table.

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:54.601
I can't get through
the sketch at table read

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:56.167
because I'm laughing so much.

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:58.267
And then, every time we run it,
I'm laughing

00:05:58.267 --> 00:05:59.734
and can't really get through it.

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:02.167
And I thought, "How am I going
to do this for the air show?"

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:05.400
Well, at dress rehearsal,
it didn't go so well.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.767
The table wasn't shaking.

00:06:06.767 --> 00:06:08.367
I got a T-bone steak
all of a sudden.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.267
Can't can't saw through
a T-Bone steak.

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:13.133
Not because it's well-done.
There's a bone in the middle.

00:06:13.133 --> 00:06:14.267
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:15.934
So, it was a --
Like, all week long,

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:17.033
everyone thought
it was going to go well.

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:18.567
But I have this
little theory that, like,

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.834
everyone thinking a sketch
is going to kill on Saturday

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:22.133
is like the kiss of death.

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:24.067
I'm like, If everyone
thinks it's going to kill,

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:25.200
it's going to tank.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.434
And that did happen
at dress rehearsal.

00:06:27.434 --> 00:06:29.367
But then -- I don't know --
Lorne had faith in it,

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:30.567
and he brought it --

00:06:30.567 --> 00:06:32.033
-And it went to air, and, man,

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:33.334
that was the best sketch
of the year.

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:34.467
Congratulations, buddy.
-Thank you.

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:35.534
-That was unbelievable.

00:06:35.534 --> 00:06:37.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:39.267
-Thank you
for coming on the show.

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:41.234
Have a great show this weekend.
Ego Nwodim.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:44.234
"Saturday Night Live"
returns this weekend

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:47.300
on NBC
and Peacock the next day,

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.367
with host Quinta Brunson
and musical guest Lil Yachty.

00:06:50.367 --> 00:06:51.367
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:52.467
Stick around.

